      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The registry is the tenant list, and it does not hold the version",
      "prov:value": "`upstream/upstream-pins.json` — in this harness's declared `upstream/`\ndirectory, and at the repository root until 2026-10-06 (bean `ar1s`) — declares\neach pinned dependency, with each `pinnedIn` resolved against the harness root:\nthe upstream repo, **the file the pin literal actually lives in**, the pattern\nthat reads it, what of ours binds to it, and the commands that constitute its\nMVP.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ar1s",
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/upstream-version-adoption.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "1 — Watch",
      "prov:value": "- **One issue, edited in place.** GitHub's own notifications are the channel\n  that was already ignored thirty times; an edit does not notify, so a pin that\n  stays stale for two months stays one unread item rather than nine."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/upstream-version-adoption.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "3 — MVP",
      "prov:value": "`site-links.ts` is the one that earns its place here: it checks the tiles\nagainst the real `_site` rather than against the attribute, which is the\ndistinction that let a 404 ship unnoticed once already."
    }
